  "raw": {
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=NYQEDG&cws=43&rid=1411": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center Job openings Frequently asked questions Internal job offers × If you are not on campus, please connect to the HEC Montreal VPN. To learn more about how the VPN works, consult the knowledge base. Access internal job offers. Job openings MENU Frequently asked questions Internal job offers New Search Login Page Position Description Faculty Position in International Business Apply Now The Department of International Business at HEC Montréal is seeking to recruit one or more professors in international business, depending on the department's needs, with expertise and interest in major global issues and the transformations of economic, social, and institutional dynamics. The committee is particularly interested in candidates whose research addresses, among other topics, international trade, global governance, the management and strategy of multinational enterprises, innovation and globalization, local/regional and national economic development, as well as new themes related to sustainable and inclusive economic development in diverse national and international contexts. Department of International Business: The Department of International Business at HEC Montréal is composed of 15 full-time faculty members from diverse disciplines. Faculty members have published their research in leading academic journals, including Technological Forecasting and Social Change , Journal of International Business Studies , Research Policy , Strategic Management Journal , Journal of Business Ethics , Journal of Management Studies , Management Science , World Development , Journal of Development Economics , Regional Studies , Journal of Economic Geography , among others. The Department offers a wide range of programs. At the undergraduate level, it offers a major and a minor in international business within the BBA and certificate programs. At the graduate level, the Department offers a large selection of courses in the MBA program, as well as in the microprogram, the Graduate Diploma (DESS), and the MSc in International Business. At the doctoral level, it offers a specialization in international business. In addition, the Department hosts the Institute for Economic Diplomacy as well as the Chair in Innovation and Regional Development. Faculty members in the Department contribute to an integrated understanding of the transformations of the global economy, combining approaches from management, economics, economic geography, and the social sciences more broadly. While rooted in the field of international business, the Department is distinguished by its interdisciplinary approach and by its increasing focus on issues of sustainability. The Department seeks primarily to recruit at the rank of Assistant Professor, ideally a recent PhD graduate or a candidate close to completing a doctorate in international business or a related field (e.g., economics, geography, political science) Responsibilities of the selected candidate include teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels, as well as advancing a research program in international business. Requirements: Candidates must have the following qualifications: A completed PhD (or near completion) in international business or a related field. Priority will be given to recent PhD graduates intending to begin their careers at the rank of Assistant Professor, although exceptional candidates at higher ranks will also be considered. A demonstrated record of, or strong potential for, scholarly research achievement. A passion for teaching and for engaging with students at different levels. Have an aptitude for teaching qualitative research methods. T he main language of instruction at HEC Montréal is French, and some courses and programs are offered in English. Proficiency in English is required to teach courses in this language, to communicate with non-French-speaking students, and to carry out certain research activities. The person must be able to teach and work in French after 2 years in the position. Substantial support will be provided by HEC Montréal to help achieve this objective, in an environment conducive to improving French language skills. It is strongly recommended to mention any prior knowledge of French in your application file. Application procedure: Interested candidates should submit as a single PDF document, before October 23, 2026 , including: curriculum vitae, a cover letter, teaching evaluations, a sample of recent publications. In their cover letter, candidates must describe their academic background and state their experience in research and teaching. They are also encouraged to describe their past contributions or future aspirations to internal and external community service. Three letters of recommendation must be submitted by the referee via this form . HEC Montréal recognizes the crucial and indispensable contribution of women, Indigenous peoples, members of visible or ethnic minorities, and persons with disabilities, and is committed to provide equal opportunities for all qualified applicants. To promote equity and excellence, the selection committee will take into account any career interruptions experienced by applicants. Applicants are invited to share the circumstances of any career interruptions and explain how these have impacted their career path. Applicants with disabilities who might need accommodations at any stage of the application process may communicate in a confidential manner dap@hec.ca . All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. We thank all applicants for their interest. However, only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now Emergency measures Follow HEC Montréal on social media Official documents Terms and conditions of use © HEC Montréal, 2026 | All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=NYQEDG&cws=43&rid=1410": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center Job openings Frequently asked questions Internal job offers × If you are not on campus, please connect to the HEC Montreal VPN. To learn more about how the VPN works, consult the knowledge base. Access internal job offers. Job openings MENU Frequently asked questions Internal job offers New Search Login Page Position Description Tenure-Track Faculty Positions in Finance (Open Rank) Apply Now The Department of Finance at HEC Montréal invites applications for two tenure-track faculty positions starting in the academic year 2027/2028. The positions are open rank: applications at the Assistant, Associate, and Full Professor levels will be given equal consideration. Candidates are sought in all areas of finance. JOB QUALIFICATIONS & DESCRIPTION • Candidates should hold a doctorate in Finance (or in a related field) or be close to the completion of their doctorate degree. • At the Assistant Professor level: candidates should be promising scholars with a well-defined research agenda. • At the Associate or Full Professor level: candidates should have an established record of publications in leading journals, demonstrated research leadership — doctoral supervision, external funding, standing in the profession — and a strong teaching record. • All successful candidates will be expected to publish research in leading journals and to teach high-quality graduate and undergraduate Finance courses. The typical teaching load for new assistant professors is 3 courses per year for the first two years. Publications are financially rewarded based on journal ranking. The main language of instruction at HEC Montréal is French, and some courses and programs are offered in English. Proficiency in English is required to teach courses in this language, to communicate with non-French-speaking students, and to carry out certain research activities. The person must be able to teach and work in French after 2 years in the position. Substantial support will be provided by HEC Montréal to help achieve this objective, in an environment conducive to improving French language skills. It is strongly recommended to mention any prior knowledge of French in your application file. APPLICATION PROCEDURE Candidates must apply online by uploading only one PDF document including: • a cover letter; • a full CV; • 1 to 3 research papers. Up to three letters of recommendation must be submitted by the recommenders via this form . Candidates applying at the Associate or Full Professor level may instead provide the names and contact details of three references at this stage; letters will only be requested later in the process and with the candidate’s consent. Applications will be considered on a rolling basis. For full consideration, the complete application file should be received no later than November 20, 2026 . Review of applications will continue until the positions are filled. ABOUT THE SCHOOL Founded in 1907, HEC Montréal is the business school affiliated with the Université de Montréal. It is the 2nd oldest business school in North America. Accredited by AACSB, AMBA, and EQUIS, HEC Montréal offers programs in finance from BBA to PhD, and boasts 36 chairs, 26 research groups, and a fully functional trading room. The Department of Finance at HEC Montréal hosts the Canadian Derivatives Institute , the Financial Education Lab , the Chair in Sustainable Finance and the Canada Research Chair in Finance and Technology . The Finance Department has 18 tenure-track faculty with a wide variety of research interests , several of whom hold a professorship or a research chair, and organizes an active seminar series . HEC Montréal recognizes the crucial and indispensable contribution of women, Indigenous peoples, members of visible or ethnic minorities, and persons with disabilities, and is committed to provide equal opportunities for all candidates. To promote equity and excellence, the selection committee will consider any career interruptions experienced by applicants. Applicants are invited to share the circumstances of any career interruptions and explain how these have impacted their career path. Applicants with disabilities who might need accommodations at any stage of the application process may communicate in a confidential manner dap@hec.ca . All candidates are encouraged to apply; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. We thank all applicants for their interest. However, only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now Emergency measures Follow HEC Montréal on social media Official documents Terms and conditions of use © HEC Montréal, 2026 | All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=NYQEDG&cws=43&rid=1414": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center Job openings Frequently asked questions Internal job offers × If you are not on campus, please connect to the HEC Montreal VPN. To learn more about how the VPN works, consult the knowledge base. Access internal job offers. Job openings MENU Frequently asked questions Internal job offers New Search Login Page Position Description Tenure-Track Professor in Project Management Apply Now The Department of Management at HEC Montréal is recruiting a tenure track Professor in Project Management (Assistant, Associate or Full). The position starts on June 1, 2027 . HEC Montréal: Founded in 1907, HEC Montreal is one of the oldest and largest business schools in North America. Over 14,000 students participate in its 160 programs, ranging from undergraduate to masters and Ph.D. as well as executive education. The school has more than 300 faculty members engaged in high quality teaching and research. HEC Montréal was the first business school in North America to obtain all three major accreditations (AACSB, EQUIS and AMBA). Its M.Sc. and MBA programs consistently rank among the best in the world. Montréal: Montréal is a welcoming, vibrant and cosmopolitan city. It is one of the safest and most affordable cities in North America. It is also a dynamic university city that attracts top talent from around the world. Montréal has a festive atmosphere, with many world-class festivals, cultural and tourist attractions. Department of Management: HEC’s Department of Management is home to more than 50 faculty members with diverse disciplinary backgrounds and specializations (management, strategy, sociology, organizational behavior, leadership, CSR, etc.). The department has a 50-year history of strong commitment to high-quality teaching, pedagogical innovation and research. It offers a broad range of courses at the MBA, B.A.A., M.Sc. and Ph.D. levels. The department also hosts several Research Chairs. Requirements: Ph.D. in Project Management, or a related field. Passion for teaching and interacting with students in various programs (B.A.A., MBA, M.Sc., Ph.D., Executive Education). Teaching experience is required (please attach your teaching evaluations). An established record of quality research and strong potential for research in Project Management. The main language of instruction at HEC Montréal is French, and some courses and programs are offered in English. Proficiency in English is required to teach courses in this language, to communicate with non-French-speaking students, and to carry out certain research activities. The person must be able to teach and work in French after 2 years in the position. Substantial support will be provided by HEC Montréal to help achieve this objective, in an environment conducive to improving French language skills. It is strongly recommended that you mention any prior knowledge of French in your application file. Application procedure: Interested candidates should submit their application online by uploading only one PDF document at the latest by November 15, 2026. Please attach a curriculum vitae, a cover letter that summarizes research and teaching experience, teaching evaluations if available, a recent publication and/or a job market paper (working paper), and a teaching and research statement (2-3 pages). In addition to applying through the portal, three letters of recommendation must be submitted by the referee via this form in order to be considered. For additional information on the requirements of the position, candidates may contact Maude Brunet, at maude.brunet@hec.ca . HEC Montréal recognizes the crucial and indispensable contribution of women, Indigenous peoples, members of visible or ethnic minorities, and persons with disabilities, and is committed to provide equal opportunities for all candidates. To promote equity and excellence, the selection committee will consider any career interruptions experienced by applicants. Applicants are invited to share the circumstances of any career interruptions and explain how these have impacted their career path. Applicants with disabilities who might need accommodations at any stage of the application process may communicate in a confidential manner at dap@hec.ca . All candidates are encouraged to apply; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. We thank all applicants for their interest. However, only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now Emergency measures Follow HEC Montréal on social media Official documents Terms and conditions of use © HEC Montréal, 2026 | All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://tre.tbe.taleo.net/tre01/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=NYQEDG&cws=43&rid=1418": {
      "title": "Position Description",
      "description": "Career Center Job openings Frequently asked questions Internal job offers × If you are not on campus, please connect to the HEC Montreal VPN. To learn more about how the VPN works, consult the knowledge base. Access internal job offers. Job openings MENU Frequently asked questions Internal job offers New Search Login Page Position Description Faculty Position in Information Technology Apply Now The Department of Information Technology (IT) at HEC Montréal is seeking to recruit an Assistant Professor in Information Technology. Outstanding candidates may be considered at higher ranks. The recruitment committee is composed of professors Benoit Aubert (chair of the committee), Ann-Frances Cameron, Wietske Van Osch, Gregory Vial, Camille Grange and Ryad Titah (Department Chair). The IT department currently has 25 faculty members (19 tenured/tenure-track and 6 teaching stream). It hosts four research chairs, four research professorships, and several active research groups (Research Group on Information Systems, ERPsim Lab, and Tech3Lab). We offer a large range of programs, including: IT major in the undergraduate Bachelor of Commerce Graduate diplomas in business analysis, digital transformation-AI, and e-business IT option in the MBA program Masters of Science (MSc) in Digital Transformation Masters of Science (MSc) in e-Commerce Masters of Science (MSc) in UX PhD in Information Technology The IT department has close links with industry and HEC Montreal is a lighthouse institution of the SAP Academic Alliance. For more information about the IT department at HEC Montreal, please visit: http://www.hec.ca/en/it/ The position will begin on June 1, 2027 . Interested candidates should upload in a single PDF the following documents prior to November 1 st , 2026 : Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement Teaching statement Three letters of recommendation must also be submitted by the referee via this form . Applicants for the position of assistant professor must have a PhD, or be near completion of a PhD in IT/MIS. They must demonstrate a strong aptitude for research, a marked interest for publication, and good teaching skills. Candidates for an Associate or Full Professor position must have attained the same rank in their current position, have an excellent publication record, and demonstrate excellence in teaching. All candidates must have a very good knowledge of technological environments and of software applications commonly used in organizations. HEC Montreal is recognized as a world leader in business education. The main language of instruction at HEC Montréal is French, and some courses and programs are offered in English. Proficiency in English is required to teach courses in this language, to communicate with non-French-speaking students, and to carry out certain research activities. The person must be able to teach and work in French after 2 years in the position. Substantial support will be provided by HEC Montréal to help achieve this objective, in an environment conducive to improving French language skills. It is strongly recommended to mention any prior knowledge of French in your application file. The typical teaching load for new assistant professors is 3 courses per year for the first two years. Please note that HEC Montreal's website is bilingual. HEC Montréal recognizes the crucial and indispensable contribution of women, Indigenous peoples, members of visible or ethnic minorities, and persons with disabilities, and is committed to provide equal opportunities for all candidates. To promote equity and excellence, the selection committee will consider any career interruptions experienced by applicants. Applicants are invited to share the circumstances of any career interruptions and explain how these have impacted their career path. Applicants with disabilities who might need accommodations at any stage of the application process may communicate in a confidential manner dap@hec.ca . All candidates are encouraged to apply; however, in accordance with Canadian immigration requirements, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. We thank all applicants for their interest. However, only those selected for an interview will be contacted. Back Share Apply Now Emergency measures Follow HEC Montréal on social media Official documents Terms and conditions of use © HEC Montréal, 2026 | All rights reserved."
    }
